Single-database configuration for Flask.

Before committing a model change, run `flask db check` and confirm it prints
"No new upgrade operations detected.":

    docker compose exec -T minerva_app_service uv run flask db check

The database is the source of truth. If the check reports a diff, change the models to
match the schema rather than generating a migration, unless the schema is genuinely wrong.
See "Schema Drift Guard" in docs/current-state/data-model.md.
